==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|lacquey}} (verb only)

===Etymology===
{{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|laquais|lang=frm}}, which is probably (via {{etyl|pro|en}} {{term|lacai|lang=pro}}?) from {{etyl|es|en}} {{term|lacayo|lang=es}}, itself perhaps from {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|lacchè|lang=it}} and {{etyl|el|en}} {{term|λακές|tr=lakés|lang=el}}, from {{etyl|tr|en}} {{term|ulak|lang=tr}}. Another possibility is through {{etyl|fr|en}}, from {{etyl|ca|en}} {{term|alacay|lang=ca}}, from {{etyl|ar|en}} {{term|قاضي|القاضي|sc=Arab|tr=al-qāḍi|lang=ar|magistrate}}. See French {{term|laquais|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{X-SAMPA|/"l{.ki/}}
* {{IPA|/ˈlæ.ki/}}
* {{rhymes|æki}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[footman]], a [[livery|liveried]] male servant.
# A [[fawn|fawning]], servile follower; a [[lickspittle]].

